    "findings": [
      "The optional boolean mask is validated and interpreted in final visible left-to-right component order.",
      "Normal terminal families select the arch on the left and terminal on the right; turned families select the terminal on the left and arch on the right.",
      "Shared-arm targets follow sorted visual axes, and bilateral spine ports map directly to left descending and right ascending ends.",
      "The long-bowl hook guard checks only the selected adjacent middle component, consistently with allocation returnContact and canonical names.",
      "Omitting the new mask preserves the established all-extended constructor path and provenance schema.",
      "Allocation tests cover all four states for each of 192 bases, unique canonical names, unchanged prior entries and display order, and local long-bowl naming.",
      "Geometry tests obtain visible-ink witnesses from baseline-pinned short and both-extended outlines and independent direction tables, rather than trusting new mask metadata alone.",
      "Preservation test design pins previous editable bytes, outlines, advances, pairs and GID order; new geometry gates check connected ink, expected counters, selected end states and source compatibility, including five compiled variable weights."
    ],
    "limitation": "This source audit reviews implementation and test design. Test execution results and complete font-build validation are recorded separately by the main task."
  },
